          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %em Kleisli category
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+a+monad"} T-algebras
            %em
              %a{:href => "algebra+over+a+monad#FreeAlgebras"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+for+a+monad"} T-algebras
            (free
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
          %p
            Explicitly one may describe (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KleisliEquivalence"}
            below) the
            %em Kleisli category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KleisliCategory"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            the objects of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            in the Kleisli category is a morphism in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to T(Y)
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            of such “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            \-shifted” morphisms.
          %p
            The Kleisli category is also characterized by the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
          %p
            Since every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            gives rise to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
            such adjunction in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor#RelationToMonads"} category of adjunctions
            for the given monad has the Kleisli category as the codomain of its left adjoint.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi T
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo ,
                  %mi μ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T} = (T,\mu,\eta)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \colon \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            with
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                multiplication
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi μ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi T
                        %mi T
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu \colon T T \to T
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi η
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi Id
                          %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta \colon Id_C \to T
          %h3#in_terms_of_free_algebras In terms of free algebras
          %p
          #FreeTAlgebras.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              A
              %strong
                free
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra over a monad
              (or free
              = succeed "-module)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T(M),\mu_M)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              is the component of multiplication transformation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mi M
                      %mo :
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_M : T(T(M))\to T(M)
            %p
          %p
          #KleisliCategory.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              The
              %strong Kleisli category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{\mathbf{T}}
              of the monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\mathbf{T}}
              on the free
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeTAlgebras"}
            %p
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U:C^{\mathbf{T}}\to C
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: C\to C^{\mathbf{T}}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+functor"} free algebra functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo :
                      %mi M
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mi M
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: M\mapsto (T M,\mu_M)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{\mathbf{T}}
              containing those objects in the image of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %h3#InTermsOfKleisliMorphisms In terms of Kleisli morphisms
          %p
            As another way of looking at this, we can keep the same objects as in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            but redefine the morphisms. This was the original Kleisli construction:
          %p
          #KleisliCategory.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              The
              %strong Kleisli category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{\mathbf{T}}
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              has:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  the objects of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mo →
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \to N
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  of the form
                #eq:KleisliMorphism.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        M \longrightarrow{\;\;} T(N)
                %p
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %strong Kleisli morphisms
            %p and
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi f
                        %mi T
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \xrightarrow{f} T N
                  with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi g
                        %mi T
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \xrightarrow{ g } T P
                  is given by the
                  %strong Kleisli composition
                  rule
                #eq:KleisliComposition.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %msub
                          %mo ∘
                          %mi Kleisli
                        %mi f
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mi P
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi f
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi M
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mi f
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ⟶
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi μ
                              %mi P
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ;
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g \circ_{Kleisli} f
                        \\;\coloneqq\;
                        \\mu_P \circ T(g) \circ f
                        \\;\colon\;
                        M
                        \\overset{f}{\longrightarrow}
                        T (N)
                        \\overset{T (g)}{\longrightarrow}
                        T \big(T (P)\big)
                        \\overset{\mu_P}{\longrightarrow}
                        T (P)
                        \\,;
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphisms"} identity morphisms
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
