            %p
              Here the triangle on the left is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+law"} unit law
              of the monad, while the commutativity of the square is the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras
            %p
              To see that the functor is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi Y
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \mapsto \mu_Y \circ T(f)
              is
