            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thunk-force+category"} thunk-force category
          %h2#references References
          %p The original articles:
          %ul
            %li#Kleisli65
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heinrich+Kleisli"}> Heinrich Kleisli
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Every standard construction is induced by a pair of adjoint functors
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 16
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/journals/proc/1965-016-03/S0002-9939-1965-0177024-4/"} ISSN0002-9939
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2034693"} jstor:2034693
            %li#Maranda66
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Marie+Maranda"}> Jean-Marie Maranda
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Fundamental Constructions and Adjoint Functors
                %strong 9
                5 (1966) 581-591 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4153/CMB-1966-072-9"}> doi:10.4153/CMB-1966-072-9
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Early accounts (together with the
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Linton"}> Fred Linton
                , §7 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An outline of functorial semantics
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seminar+on+Triples+and+Categorical+Homology+Theory"} Seminar on Triples and Categorical Homology Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 80
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0083080"} doi:10.1007/BFb0083080
            %li#MacLane71
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                , §VI.5 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
                %strong 5
                Springer (1971) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"}> doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Wells"} Charles Wells
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toposes%2C+Triples%2C+and+Theories"} Toposes, Triples, and Theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 278
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/12/tr12abs.html"} TAC:12
            %li
              %p
                Jenö Szigeti,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On limits and colimits in the Kleisli category
                %strong 24
                4 (1983) 381-391 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=CTGDC_1983__24_4_381_0"}> numdam:CTGDC_1983__24_4_381_0
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
            over a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Kleisli+category"} co-Kleisli category
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            (if it exists):
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Kleiner"}> Mark Kleiner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Adjoint monads and an isomorphism of the Kleisli categories
              %strong 133
              1 (1990) 79-82 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0021-8693(90)90069-Z"}> doi:10.1016/0021-8693(90)90069-Z
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The terminology “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+triple"}> Kleisli triple
            ” for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            presented as an “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension+system"}> extension system
            ” and relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation"} computation
            with effects (see at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+in+computer+science"} monads in computer science
          %ul
            %li#Moggi91
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eugenio+Moggi"}> Eugenio Moggi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notions of computation and monads
              %strong 93
              1 (1991) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0890-5401(91)90052-4"}> doi:10.1016/0890-5401(91)90052-4
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.disi.unige.it/person/MoggiE/ftp/ic91.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Textbook account making explicit the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+equivalence"} Kleisli equivalence
          %ul
            %li#Borceux94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
              , pp. 191 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categories and Structures
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 50
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511525865"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511525865
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"}> Thomas Streicher
              , pp. 54 in:
              %em Introduction to Category Theory and Categorical Logic
              (2003) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www2.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~streicher/CTCL.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Streicher-CategoryTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of cases where the inclusion of the Kleisli category into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            is a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcelo+Fiore"}> Marcelo Fiore
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matias+Menni"} Matias Menni
              = succeed "," do
                %em Reflective Kleisli subcategories of the category of Eilenberg-Moore algebras for factorization monads
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/15/2/15-02abs.html"} TAC
          %p#TwoSidedReferences
            Discussion of combined “double” or “two-sided” Kleisli categories, combining the Kleisli category of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Kleisli+category"} co-Kleisli category
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+law"} distributes
            over it:
          %ul
            %li#BrookesVanStone93
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephen+Brookes"}> Stephen Brookes
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kathryn+Van+Stone"} Kathryn Van Stone
              %em Monads and Comonads in Intensional Semantics
              (1993) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://apps.dtic.mil/sti/citations/ADA266522"}> dtic:ADA266522
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~brookes/papers/MonadsComonads.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BrookesVanStone-CoMonads.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and generalization to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monads"} 2-monads
          %ul
            %li#Garner08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"}> Richard Garner
              , pp. 11 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Polycategories via pseudo-distributive laws
              %strong 218
              3 (2008) 781-827 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0606735"}> arXiv:0606735
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2008.02.001"} doi:10.1016/j.aim.2008.02.001
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
            theory:
          %ul
            %li
              Tomasz Brzeziński, Adrian Vazquez-Marquez,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Internal Kleisli categories
              %strong 215
              9 (2011) 213-147 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.4048"}> arXiv:0911.4048
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion in a context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+systems+theory"} categorical systems theory
          %ul
            %li#MyersBook
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Jaz+Myers"}> David Jaz Myers
              , §2.3 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categorical systems theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/DavidJaz/DynamicalSystemsBook/tree/master/book"} github
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://davidjaz.com/Papers/DynamicalBook.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of Kleisli categories in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Simpson"}> Alex Simpson
              ,
              %em Recursive types in Kleisli Categories
              (
              %a{:href => "https://www.research.ed.ac.uk/en/publications/recursive-types-in-kleisli-categories"}> pdf
              )
        .revisedby
